WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.080
Caster: "This is when bengi has to step up to save SKT"

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:08.560
Caster: "On blue side, remember with bengi in they do not have a Nidalee player. You cannot give Peanut Nidalee.

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:13.020
We talked about how you need adaptation and now you're forced to ban Nidalee on Blue side.

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:18.960
This could be the last game of the night or if bengi has anything to say, we go to a game five."

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:27.340
Already a two-time World Champion, Bengi was
supposedly over the hill.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:29.800
But Bengi was a World Champion.

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:33.579
And with everything on the line, SKT needed
a win.

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:39.140
A veteran voice to show them the path to victory. They
needed Bengi.

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:42.400
After all, they’ve never won Worlds without him.

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:47.000
This is Bengi’s story

00:00:51.580 --> 00:01:00.040
Bae “Bengi” Seong-woong was born on November 21, 1994 and not much is known about his life
before League of Legends.

00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:04.650
Bengi’s first recorded games were on an
amateur team called BBT, which played in a

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:06.990
Korean secondary league known as NLB.

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:12.120
On that team, he played alongside legendary
support player Cho “Mata” Se-hyeong.

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:16.360
(Casting)

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:21.260
After the team disbanded, bengi ended up at
a tryout for SK Telecom’s new sister team,

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:23.329
SK Telecom T1 K.

00:01:23.329 --> 00:01:27.520
And though he left midway because he felt
he wasn’t good enough to make the team,

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:32.390
coach Kim “kkOma” Jeong-gyun saw something
great in the young jungler and managed to

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:38.460
pull him back. SKT was built around a young
solo queue star that was turning heads at

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:41.020
the time, Lee “Faker” Sang-hyeok.

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:49.080
(Casting)

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:53.220
The team was designed to be aggressive, capitalizing
on Faker’s playstyle.

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:54.240
It worked.

00:01:54.240 --> 00:02:05.720
(Casting)

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:11.560
SKT’s sister team placed third in Champions
Spring, and posted impressive results in their

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:12.740
debut season.

00:02:12.740 --> 00:02:16.000
But more importantly, they had the potential
to be great .

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:24.460
MonteCristo: "All aboard the Korean hype train, SK Telecom T1."

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:30.610
The team went 12-4 in the summer season and
qualified for Worlds 2013 where they swept

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:35.000
Royal Club in the Grand Finals to take home
their first world championship.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:44.120
(Casting)

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:50.200
SKT returned home to Korea as champions, and
they didn’t slow down for even a second.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:03:07.880
(Casting)

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:13.280
SKT won Champions Winter with a perfect record and were

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:17.000
without a doubt the best team in the world.

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:34.160
But amidst all the success, few noticed Bengi’s
playstyle slowly shifting.

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:40.099
His early game aggression, a hallmark of SKT’s
fast-paced bulldozer playstyle, gave way to

00:03:40.099 --> 00:03:42.000
something more supportive.

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:59.550
Bengi was Faker’s invisible guardian.

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:04.090
He was the man who set up Faker for the flashy
plays that have made him legendary.

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:08.320
There’s no question that Faker was the best,
but he couldn’t have done it without Bengi.

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:12.400
After Champions Winter, SKT started to crumble.

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:18.000
They placed fourth in Champions Spring, and
were then swept in a tiebreaker match against

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:22.660
Samsung White which forced them to play in
the Regional Finals, where they would eventually

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:25.200
lose to NaJin White Shield 3-1.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:35.760
(Casting)

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:41.180
Just a few months prior, SKT were the reigning
World Champions with a perfect record in their

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:42.190
home region.

00:04:42.190 --> 00:04:44.380
But they couldn’t keep up.

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:48.820
Bengi wasn’t solely blamed for the team’s
struggles, but the common perception was that

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:54.000
Faker, the greatest player on earth, just
couldn’t carry his entire team.

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:15.600
SKT rebuilt in the offseason, shedding everyone
except for Faker and Bengi.

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:18.670
The god and his right hand man.

00:05:18.670 --> 00:05:21.760
But even so, people were ready to write off
Bengi.

00:05:21.760 --> 00:05:26.250
He was part of a roster that not even Faker
could carry, and his mechanics were seen as

00:05:26.250 --> 00:05:28.040
being out of date.

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:33.000
Younger players were faster, more adaptable,
and had deeper champion pools.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:38.980
(Casting)

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:41.240
In 2015, SKT

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:46.740
signed Im “T0M” Jae-hyeon as a substitute
for Bengi, and swapped between the two junglers

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:48.090
throughout the season.

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:53.190
What was telling though, was the fact that
SKT elected to play Bengi for all three games

00:05:53.190 --> 00:05:56.190
of their finals series against the GE Tigers.

00:05:56.190 --> 00:05:59.000
A series SKT went on to win 3-0.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:25.760
(Casting)

00:06:26.020 --> 00:06:30.831
In interviews, Bengi said that watching T0M
play helped him regain his confidence after

00:06:30.831 --> 00:06:32.950
his abysmal 2014 season.

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:34.270
That’s right.

00:06:34.270 --> 00:06:39.260
Bengi, the guy who walked out of tryouts only
to be pulled back in, needed a rookie to remind

00:06:39.260 --> 00:06:41.420
himself how good he could be.

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:07.020
SKT went on to win the summer season, punching
their ticket to Worlds in the process.

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:13.350
Fortunately for Bengi, SKT took mid lane substitute,
Lee "Easyhoon" Ji-hoon to the tournament,

00:07:13.350 --> 00:07:17.950
meaning that Bengi was the only jungler the
team would field at Worlds.

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:23.710
SKT went on to win the tournament, giving
Faker and Bengi their second world championship

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:25.000
in three years.

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:37.880
(Casting)

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:43.500
But even with a second world championship under
his belt, people still kept harping on Bengi.

00:07:54.180 --> 00:08:00.630
Ahead of the Spring 2016 season, SKT signed
Kang "Blank" Sun-gu, and started him for most

00:08:00.630 --> 00:08:02.400
of the regular season.

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:08.690
Bengi only played in 17 of SKT’s 41 games
in the spring, and rode the bench throughout

00:08:08.720 --> 00:08:09.800
the playoffs.

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:15.060
Caster: "I wish I could have been watching their scrims. Watching them decide between Blank and Bengi

00:08:15.060 --> 00:08:19.800
because from what we've seen both of them have been pretty poor."

00:08:19.800 --> 00:08:22.980
SKT started Bengi more often in the summer, but

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:28.820
as the season wore on, Bengi lost more and
more and was benched after just 14 games.

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:32.200
Again, Blank played in the playoffs instead
of Bengi.

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:38.880
Caster: "Blank, the one thing you can say about him, has stepped up when he's needed to. You think back to LCK final you think back to MSI final.

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:41.340
He was good in those series and he's gonna need to be good today"

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:49.300
SKT took Bengi with them to Worlds in 2016,
but he only played in two games during the

00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:50.700
group stage.

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:56.200
SKT started Bengi against Royal in the quarterfinals,
but after losing Game 1, quickly subbed him

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:57.080
out for Blank.

00:08:57.080 --> 00:09:03.480
Jatt: "I like the substitution for them. I think Blank has been their go-to for the majority of the season and I was surprised whenever we would see Bengi.

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:07.520
If they weren't going to make it a permanent thing I thought it was because of his world championship experience.

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:14.820
But this SKT team has won the IEM World Championship with Blank, they won MSI with Blank and I think if they want to win they should be doing it with Blank."

00:09:14.920 --> 00:09:20.960
The writing seemed to be on the wall for Bengi:
he was still good, but no longer great.

00:09:22.680 --> 00:09:27.000
But in Game 4 of the semifinals, SKT were
on the ropes.

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:31.960
Jatt: "SKT have to change things up in this next one because they tried round two of the Miss Fortune lane,

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:33.300
they lost again. They have to change."

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:37.060
And with everything on the line, SKT needed a win.

00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:38.860
That's when they called in Bengi

00:09:38.860 --> 00:11:54.000
(Casting)

00:11:54.360 --> 00:12:01.000
Bengi started in four of SKT’s Grand Final games
against Samsung Galaxy, going 3-1 and notching

00:12:01.040 --> 00:12:07.860
his and Faker’s third World Championship
in five year, cementing SKT’s legacy

00:12:07.880 --> 00:12:11.000
as League of Legends’ first dynasty.

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:19.000
(Casting)

00:12:24.040 --> 00:12:29.950
Surely the entire world would finally see
that when Bengi is sitting next to Faker,

00:12:29.950 --> 00:12:33.279
no team in the world could stop them.

00:12:33.280 --> 00:12:38.300
But Bengi is always doomed to be the bridesmaid,
and never the bride.

00:12:38.340 --> 00:12:41.760
He’s invisible and most importantly he's not Faker.

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:58.040
SKT dropped bengi in 2017 and replaced him
with the Tigers’ star jungler Han “Peanut”

00:12:58.040 --> 00:12:59.120
Wang-ho.

00:12:59.120 --> 00:13:03.690
Bengi went off to Vici Gaming in China, where
he ended up losing a relegation match and

00:13:03.690 --> 00:13:05.160
being dropped from that team too.

00:13:05.160 --> 00:13:12.200
(Casting)

00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:17.920
SKT had a strong 2017, placing first in the
Spring Playoffs and second in the summer,

00:13:17.920 --> 00:13:21.000
but they didn’t look dominant going into
Worlds.

00:13:24.940 --> 00:13:42.800
(Casting)

00:13:44.660 --> 00:13:51.350
SKT placed second at Worlds in 2017, which
marked their first ever loss in a Worlds Grand

00:13:51.350 --> 00:13:52.520
Finals series.

00:13:52.520 --> 00:13:56.000
Their first time playing at the tournament
without Bengi.

00:13:59.360 --> 00:14:08.200
YamatoCannon: "It's insane what they did, knowing that they've won three world championships, expecting to win four is natural because of

00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:14.600
the dominant streak that they've had, but in all seriousness what they've accomplished, no one is going to come close to this

00:14:14.600 --> 00:14:20.420
or sure something is quite close to this with the two victories but in theory it's still incredible what they did.

00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:28.760
And maybe it takes one year, maybe it takes two years for them to come back to that same form, but kkOma knows the recipe to success.

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:32.060
SKT knows the recipe for success within League."

00:14:32.080 --> 00:14:38.300
It’s impossible to say exactly how much
bengi impacted SKT’s playstyle, and whether

00:14:38.300 --> 00:14:42.100
or not he completely altered the way SKT treats
junglers moving forwards.

00:14:43.080 --> 00:14:47.120
But he’s returned to SKT, this time as a coach. Bengi and Faker have

00:14:47.130 --> 00:14:48.260
been reunited.

00:14:48.260 --> 00:14:53.400
While Bengi is playing an even more supportive,
invisible role this time around, one thing

00:14:53.400 --> 00:14:59.110
will always remain true: when the unkillable
demon king has bengi by his side, nothing

00:14:59.110 --> 00:15:01.000
can stop SKT.

